searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Lattice","doc":"High-level Elixir interface for the Lattice DSL runtime.","ref":"Lattice.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Lattice","doc":"# Create a runtime\n    {:ok, rt} = Lattice.new()\n\n    # Evaluate expressions\n    {:ok, 6} = Lattice.eval(rt, \"1 + 2 + 3\")\n    {:ok, \"hello world\"} = Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(\"hello\" + \" \" + \"world\"))\n\n    # Define and call functions\n    Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(\n      def add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {\n        a + b\n      }\n    ))\n    {:ok, 7} = Lattice.call(rt, \"add\", [3, 4])\n\n    # Define types and use them\n    Lattice.eval(rt, \"type Person { name: String, age: Int }\")\n    {:ok, person} = Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(Person { name: \"Alice\", age: 30 }))\n    # person is %{\"name\" => \"Alice\", \"age\" => 30}","ref":"Lattice.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Value Marshaling - Lattice","doc":"Values are automatically converted between Elixir and Lattice:\n\n| Lattice Type | Elixir Type |\n|--------------|-------------|\n| null         | :null atom  |\n| Bool         | boolean     |\n| Int          | integer     |\n| Float        | float       |\n| String       | binary      |\n| Path         | {:path, binary} |\n| List         | list        |\n| Map          | map         |","ref":"Lattice.html#module-value-marshaling"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.call/3","doc":"Call a Lattice function by name.","ref":"Lattice.html#call/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Lattice.call/3","doc":"# First define a function\n    Lattice.eval(rt, \"def double(x: Int) -> Int { x * 2 }\")\n\n    # Then call it\n    {:ok, 10} = Lattice.call(rt, \"double\", [5])","ref":"Lattice.html#call/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.eval/2","doc":"Evaluate Lattice source code.\n\nReturns `{:ok, value}` on success or `{:error, reason}` on failure.","ref":"Lattice.html#eval/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Lattice.eval/2","doc":"{:ok, 42} = Lattice.eval(rt, \"40 + 2\")\n    {:ok, \"hello\"} = Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(\"hello\"))\n    {:ok, [1, 2, 3]} = Lattice.eval(rt, \"[1, 2, 3]\")","ref":"Lattice.html#eval/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.eval_with_bindings/3","doc":"Evaluate with pre-bound variables.","ref":"Lattice.html#eval_with_bindings/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Lattice.eval_with_bindings/3","doc":"{:ok, 30} = Lattice.eval_with_bindings(rt, \"x + y\", [{\"x\", 10}, {\"y\", 20}])","ref":"Lattice.html#eval_with_bindings/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.get_function_signatures/1","doc":"Get all function signatures.\n\nReturns a list of function signature maps with name, params,\nreturn type, and metadata (is_llm, is_async).","ref":"Lattice.html#get_function_signatures/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.get_global/2","doc":"Get a global variable.\n\nReturns `{:ok, value}` if found, `{:error, :not_found}` otherwise.","ref":"Lattice.html#get_global/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.get_types/1","doc":"Get all registered type schemas.\n\nReturns a list of type schema maps that can be used to generate\nElixir structs or validate data.","ref":"Lattice.html#get_types/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.has_function?/2","doc":"Check if a function exists.","ref":"Lattice.html#has_function?/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.new/0","doc":"Create a new Lattice runtime.\n\nThe runtime is isolated - it has its own globals, functions, and types.","ref":"Lattice.html#new/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.new_with_llm/0","doc":"Create a new Lattice runtime with LLM support.\n\nRequires OPENROUTER_API_KEY environment variable to be set.","ref":"Lattice.html#new_with_llm/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.reset/1","doc":"Reset the runtime, clearing all state.","ref":"Lattice.html#reset/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.set_global/3","doc":"Set a global variable.","ref":"Lattice.html#set_global/3"},{"type":"module","title":"Lattice.Native","doc":"NIF bindings for the Lattice runtime.\n\nThis module provides low-level access to the Lattice runtime through\nprecompiled Rustler NIFs. For most use cases, use the higher-level `Lattice` module.","ref":"Lattice.Native.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.call_function/3","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#call_function/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.eval/2","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#eval/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.eval_file/2","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#eval_file/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.eval_with_base_path/3","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#eval_with_base_path/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.eval_with_bindings/3","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#eval_with_bindings/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.get_function_signatures/1","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#get_function_signatures/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.get_global/2","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#get_global/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.get_types/1","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#get_types/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.has_function/2","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#has_function/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.new_runtime/0","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#new_runtime/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.new_runtime_with_llm/0","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#new_runtime_with_llm/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.reset/1","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#reset/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Lattice.Native.set_global/3","doc":"","ref":"Lattice.Native.html#set_global/3"},{"type":"extras","title":"Lattice","doc":"# Lattice\n\nElixir bindings for the Lattice DSL runtime - a domain-specific language with LLM integration.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Lattice","doc":"Add `lattice` to your list of dependencies in `mix.exs`:\n\n```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:lattice, \"~> 0.1.0\"}\n  ]\nend\n```\n\n**Note**: This package currently only supports macOS Apple Silicon (aarch64-apple-darwin).","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Usage - Lattice","doc":"```elixir\n# Create a runtime\n{:ok, rt} = Lattice.new()\n\n# Evaluate expressions\n{:ok, 6} = Lattice.eval(rt, \"1 + 2 + 3\")\n{:ok, \"hello world\"} = Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(\"hello\" + \" \" + \"world\"))\n\n# Define and call functions\nLattice.eval(rt, \"\"\"\n  def add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {\n    a + b\n  }\n\"\"\")\n{:ok, 7} = Lattice.call(rt, \"add\", [3, 4])\n\n# Define types\nLattice.eval(rt, \"type Person { name: String, age: Int }\")\n{:ok, person} = Lattice.eval(rt, ~s(Person { name: \"Alice\", age: 30 }))\n# => %{\"name\" => \"Alice\", \"age\" => 30}\n\n# Use with bindings\n{:ok, 30} = Lattice.eval_with_bindings(rt, \"x + y\", [{\"x\", 10}, {\"y\", 20}])\n```","ref":"readme.html#usage"},{"type":"extras","title":"Building from source - Lattice","doc":"If you need to compile the NIF locally (requires Rust toolchain):\n\n```bash\nLATTICE_BUILD=true mix deps.compile lattice --force\n```","ref":"readme.html#building-from-source"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Lattice","doc":"MIT","ref":"readme.html#license"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.39.2"}}